First, define your base model that all your tables will inherit from:

```python
from django.db import models
from django.utils.functional import cached_property

class BaseModel(models.Model):
    class Meta:
        abstract = True

    @cached_property
    def _get_fields(self):
        return {field.name: getattr(self, field.name) for field in self._meta.get_fields()}

    def __str__(self):
        return str(self._get_fields())
```

In this example, we define a `BaseModel` which has an abstract meta-class and a cached property `_get_fields` that returns a dictionary of all the fields and their values for the current instance.

