Here's an R function that takes a character vector as input and returns `TRUE` if all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric, otherwise it returns `FALSE`. The function uses the `tryCatch()` function to catch any conversion errors and returns `FALSE` if such errors occur.

```R
isNumericVector <- function(x) {
  is.numeric <- TRUE
  for (i in seq_along(x)) {
    if (is.na(x[i])) next
    tryCatch({
      x[i] <- as.numeric(x[i])
    }, error = function(e) {
      is.numeric <- FALSE
      return(FALSE)
    })
  }
  is.numeric
}
```

Let's test this function with some examples:

```R
# Test cases
x1 <- c("1", "2", "3", NA, "4")
x2 <- c("1", "a", "3", NA, "4")
x3 <- c(1, 2, 3, NA, 4)

isNumericVector(x1)
# [1] TRUE

isNumericVector(x2)
# [1] FALSE

isNumericVector(x3)
# [1] TRUE
```

In the first example, `x1`, all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric, so the function returns `TRUE`. In the second example, `x2`, not all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric, so the function returns `FALSE`. In the third example, `x3`, all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric, so the function returns `TRUE` again.

```typescript
import { Injectable, NestMiddleware } from 'nestjs';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';
import { map } from 'rxjs/operators';

@Injectable()
export class EnvMiddleware implements NestMiddleware {
  constructor() {}

  use(req: any, res: any, next: () => void): Observable<any> {
    const env = process.env.NODE_ENV;

    if (env === 'production') {
      return next().pipe(map(() => null)); // Return null to skip further processing
    } else {
      return next();
    }
  }
}
```

To use this decorator, add the following line in your `main.ts` file after importing the middleware:

```typescript
app.use(new EnvMiddleware());
```

This decorator checks the value of the `NODE_ENV` environment variable and skips further processing by returning `null` if the environment is set to production (`'production'`). Otherwise, it continues with the normal request flow. By returning `null`, we're indicating that no response body needs to be sent back to the client.

In development mode, the request will continue as usual, and the response body will be sent back to the client. However, in production mode, the request will be terminated immediately after executing the middleware. This can help improve performance and reduce server load during production.

